{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\ne=d['experiment']\ne['previous_id']='ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-experiment'\ne['revision_reason']='Only the comparison declaration changes: identity_fields are reduced to the case selector (mode) so the startup_before_restart admission and the restart_after_recovery result share an identity; the harness, inputs and assertions are unchanged. The previous receipt correlated neither admission to a result, so its comparisons returned unknown even though the raw events were emitted.'\nfor c in e['comparisons']:\n    c['identity_fields']=['mode']\nd['interpretations']=[{\n 'investigation_id':'ef5ddbf78bd4456ea51537bd60a61a80-question-0',\n 'source_ids':['api_restore_committed_call','api_restore_committed_body','api_restore_snapshot_config','raft_follower_election_abort','raft_quorum_size','raft_processlogs_prepare'],\n 'executions':{'99b89f1a9b634301a58130e5494d394f':[0,1,2,3]},\n 'conclusion':'conditional',\n 'defect_claim':'asserted',\n 'rationale':'The retained receipt 99b89f1a9b634301a58130e5494d394f (exit 0) contains the four emitted events, and the two result events witness the predicted difference under identical inputs: event 1 (mode on, restore_committed_logs true, snapshots 0) reports after_latest_index 0, after_servers 0, after_has_vote false with after_commit_index 11 and after_last_applied 11, while event 3 (mode off) reports after_latest_index 1, after_servers 1, after_has_vote true. The admission events (0 and 2) confirm both cases started from before_latest_index 1 with one server, so the only difference is whether restoreFromCommittedLogs advanced lastApplied. Source reading explains the mechanism: NewRaft starts with an empty configurations struct, restoreSnapshot (api.go:655-681) is the only persistent-state producer of a configuration, and the startup log scan (api.go:610-613) is the only other producer but begins at max(snapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1; restoreFromCommittedLogs (api.go:724-754) runs first and sets lastApplied to the persisted commit index, so committed LogConfiguration entries at or below it are skipped, and processLogs never updates r.configurations (raft.go:1366-1391). The receipt s declared comparisons returned unknown rather than violated: the controller reported \\\"No corresponding prerequisite events reached: mode_on/startup_before_restart\\\" for both on-case comparisons and the analogous message for the off-case control, because the compared identity included phase and the admission events carry phase before_restart while the result events carry after_restart. That is a declaration defect, not missing evidence, so the raw observations are retained and a successor experiment with identity_fields [mode] is submitted for a fresh, complete comparison; no completed comparison is claimed here. Consequence under the stated conditions: the restarted node holds an empty (or snapshot-age) membership view, so runFollower\\\\'s \\\"no known peers, aborting election\\\" branch (raft.go:228-232) and the hasVote gate (raft.go:236-246) leave it unable to campaign, and quorumSize() (raft.go:1087-1094) is computed over a configuration that contradicts its own committed log.',\n 'counterevidence':['A restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps the configuration (event 3), which isolates the flagged recovery path rather than the restart itself.','A snapshot can supply a configuration (api.go:677-678), but only as of snapshot.ConfigurationIndex, which cannot cover a configuration committed after that snapshot.'],\n 'limitations':['The comparison outcomes in this receipt are unknown; a completed comparison waits on the successor experiment.','Only the single-node, no-snapshot case is witnessed; the snapshot-present variant remains the registered gap.','The separate suspicion that restoreFromCommittedLogs\\\\' processLogs call can block NewRaft before runFSM starts is untested and outside this claim.']\n}]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('patched')\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
